Subject: [PATCH] gix-command: fuzz: don't Debug-format the prepared Command

The prepare fuzzer formatted each of the six std::process::Command values
it builds per input with `format!("{command:?}")`. That runs std's
Command/OsString Debug code (escape_debug per character), not gix-command,
and was most of the time per input. Pass the Result to black_box instead,
so the Command is still built and observed. No assertion depended on the
string. No open upstream PR or issue touches gix-command/fuzz (gh search,
2026-11-20).

diff --git a/gix-command/fuzz/fuzz_targets/prepare.rs b/gix-command/fuzz/fuzz_targets/prepare.rs
index d038a06..5ea7e2c 100644
--- a/gix-command/fuzz/fuzz_targets/prepare.rs
+++ b/gix-command/fuzz/fuzz_targets/prepare.rs
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ fn inspect_prepare(command: &str) {
         gix_command::prepare(command).with_shell().with_quoted_command(),
     ] {
         let command = std::process::Command::try_from(prep);
-        _ = black_box(format!("{command:?}"));
+        _ = black_box(command);
     }
 }
 
